    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "But these meetings are generally with a purpose. And anytime I travel abroad, it's about security. It's about prosperity, global security, global prosperity, lifting up people. And it's about governance. It's about integrity and honesty. fighting corruption, et cetera, which causes problems. And so in this most recent, the G7, which I just got back from a couple of days ago, our focus was on climate and the oceans and how we, as multilateralists, come together to work together to save the planet. There's no question, though, when you're among your colleagues, other speakers, presidents of parliaments, as they mostly call them, that they want to know about our country. And they're not shy about saying that they're concerned about America's, shall we say, change in leadership in the world, taking responsibility for leadership in the world. And they all want us to know that everybody depends on the United States to being a leader in the world.",
