    "turn_text": "about Donald Trump, but we do have concerns about many issues, including climate, where we're in denial. The president said he's not going to use science as the basis for any decisions about the environment or the endangered species or climate or anything like that. That's strange, and so we can differentiate from the administration in terms of policies of the House Democrats on those subjects. So we can disagree, but not to have a conversation about the current occupant of the White House. The other part of it, though, that I think is interesting is that, you know, for example, we have the issue of Afghanistan right now, and that is that we all went in together. We all went in together. NATO countries all went in together. And now the president's leaving alone. You know, he really must consult with them more. And those kinds of interactions raise questions and concern.",
