    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73245.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "It's curious to me that he wrote that article. It is expected us to bring up a bill that is a treaty that is not complete, that has no assurances that our workers in our country and in other countries will be respected and protected. Does it have no concern about what it means in terms of the environment or no concerns and what it means in terms of enforceability and prescription drug issues? So to say, bring up a bill is like, what are you talking about? Do you know what you're talking about? What we're talking about is we're trying to be on a path to yes, we have to find our common ground. But if you have a bill that is not in a treaty that's not enforceable, you're just fooling the public. You're just fooling the public. We think we can get to enforceability. It doesn't help that people say just bring up a bill because it'll pass.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
