    "turn_text": "That's nothing. We're not bringing it up. We'll bring it up when we're ready. And when the bill is ready. And right now we're in negotiation about enforceability. I myself voted for NAFTA. 1.0. And it was disappointing in terms of enforceability. Some areas of our country benefited. Some areas did not. But I think if it had better enforcement, we would have had more benefits for more workers. I don't want to see an after 2.0, as you call it, something that just drives Mexican workers into poverty. as it exploits US workers. We want to lift up all workers in our country and others in Canada as well. And I say lift up and sustain a level of participation that has them be able to raise their families and the rest. So again, we have work to do. We are on a path. We're working to get it done. But I don't know what the point is of saying, bring a bill to the floor where you do not have not concluded the negotiations.",
